From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:47:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: Optionally stop busy CPUs pulling misfit
 tasks

With MISFIT_ROTATE, CPU-bound tasks on an asymmetric system share the
CPUs of the highest capacity by swaps. Each such task then spends part
of its time on a smaller CPU, so its utilization settles well below the
big CPU's capacity: ten threads on four big and six small CPUs run on
the big ones about 40 % of the time.

update_sd_pick_busiest() lets a CPU pull a misfit task only while its
own group has spare capacity, and group_has_capacity() decides that
from utilization. Four busy big CPUs whose tasks average that lower
utilization classify as group_has_spare, and dst_core_idle is always
true without SMT. A busy big CPU therefore picks the small CPUs' group
as group_misfit_task, active balance moves a running task onto the big
CPU, and two tasks share one big CPU while a small CPU has none, until
balancing moves a task back down.

On a T8132 (4 + 6 CPUs) running linux-aurora-next 1.1117, ten
CPU-bound threads showed two threads on one CPU and an empty small CPU
in 4 of 15 one-second samples, and reached 96.5 % of the throughput
macOS reaches on the same machine at the same clocks.

Add a debugfs knob, misfit_pull_idle. With 1, while MISFIT_ROTATE is
on, a busy destination does not pull a misfit task; an idle one still
does, so a misfit task still moves up to an idle big CPU, and the swaps
alone share busy big CPUs. The default, 0, keeps today's behaviour.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 kernel/sched/debug.c |  1 +
 kernel/sched/fair.c  | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 kernel/sched/sched.h |  1 +
 3 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/debug.c b/kernel/sched/debug.c
index ce09352d83..68e32f75ff 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/debug.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/debug.c
@@ -733,6 +733,7 @@ static __init int sched_init_debug(void)
 	debugfs_create_u32("fork_big_lift", 0644, debugfs_sched, &sysctl_sched_fork_big_lift);
 	debugfs_create_u32("fork_big_gap_ns", 0644, debugfs_sched, &sysctl_sched_fork_big_gap);
 	debugfs_create_u32("misfit_new_ns", 0644, debugfs_sched, &sysctl_sched_misfit_new);
+	debugfs_create_u32("misfit_pull_idle", 0644, debugfs_sched, &sysctl_sched_misfit_pull_idle);
 
 	sched_domains_mutex_lock();
 	update_sched_domain_debugfs();
diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index 904435f76e..48a6943e5e 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -119,6 +119,17 @@ __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_fork_big_gap;
  */
 __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_misfit_new	= 1000000UL;
 
+/*
+ * misfit_pull_idle: with MISFIT_ROTATE, CPU-bound tasks share the CPUs of the
+ * highest capacity by swaps, so their utilization stays below that capacity
+ * and a group of busy big CPUs can classify as group_has_spare. A busy big CPU
+ * then pulls a misfit task by active balance and leaves the smaller CPU it ran
+ * on without a task. 1: while MISFIT_ROTATE is on, only an idle CPU pulls a
+ * misfit task, and busy big CPUs are shared by the swaps alone.
+ * (default: 0 = off; a debugfs knob because the feature mask is full)
+ */
+__read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_misfit_pull_idle;
+
 static int __init setup_sched_thermal_decay_shift(char *str)
 {
 	pr_warn("Ignoring the deprecated sched_thermal_decay_shift= option\n");
@@ -12518,6 +12529,16 @@ static inline void update_sg_lb_stats(struct lb_env *env,
 				sgs->group_capacity;
 }
 
+/*
+ * misfit_pull_idle: a busy destination does not pull a misfit task while the
+ * swaps of MISFIT_ROTATE share the big CPUs. An idle one still does.
+ */
+static inline bool misfit_pull_busy_dst(struct lb_env *env)
+{
+	return READ_ONCE(sysctl_sched_misfit_pull_idle) &&
+	       sched_feat(MISFIT_ROTATE) && env->idle == __CPU_NOT_IDLE;
+}
+
 /**
  * update_sd_pick_busiest - return 1 on busiest group
  * @env: The load balancing environment.
@@ -12557,7 +12578,8 @@ static bool update_sd_pick_busiest(struct lb_env *env,
 	    (sgs->group_type == group_misfit_task) &&
 	    (!env->dst_core_idle ||
 	     !capacity_greater(capacity_of(env->dst_cpu), sg->sgc->max_capacity) ||
-	     sds->local_stat.group_type != group_has_spare))
+	     sds->local_stat.group_type != group_has_spare ||
+	     misfit_pull_busy_dst(env)))
 		return false;
 
 	/*
diff --git a/kernel/sched/sched.h b/kernel/sched/sched.h
index f9908fccbb..7fcecb45d3 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/sched.h
+++ b/kernel/sched/sched.h
@@ -3162,6 +3162,7 @@ extern __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_misfit_runtime;
 extern __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_fork_big_lift;
 extern __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_fork_big_gap;
 extern __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_misfit_new;
+extern __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_misfit_pull_idle;
 
 extern unsigned int sysctl_sched_base_slice;
 
-- 
2.43.0

